<title>USA: LIPA plans fixed, floating-rate debt in LILCO pact.</title>
<headline>LIPA plans fixed, floating-rate debt in LILCO pact.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Long Island Power Authority (LIPA), which wants to buy assets from Brooklyn Union Gas Co and Long Island Lighting Co, on Wednesday said that it planned to sell both fixed-rate and floating-rate debt to pay for the transaction.</p>
<p>The first $4.297 billion issue of tax-free bonds, which would be sold after the transaction is completed, would be comprised of $1.3 billion of fixed-rate insured bonds, $1.997 billion of fixed-rate uninsured bonds and $1 billion of floating-rate bonds.</p>
</text>
